.TH DELBAK 1.SH NAMEdelbak \- delete backup files in a directory tree.SH SYNOPSIS\fBdelbak\fR[\-nl] [\-f=ext] [directory].SH DESCRIPTION\fBdelbak\fRremoves every file whose name ends in\fB_bak\fRfrom a directory, the current one unless named, and from everydirectory beneath it..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-l\fRlist the files that would go, and remove nothing..TP 12\fB\-n\fRthis directory only, no recursion..TP 12\fB\-f=\fIext\fRremove files ending in\fIext\fRinstead of\fB_bak\fR.\fR.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOrm, find